{"assignees":[{"id":"U_kgDOD0cnBQ","login":"Adraca","name":"Adraca Ai Private Ltd","databaseId":256321285}],"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTg1NDg2","is_bot":false,"login":"thenoahhein","name":"Noah Hein"},"body":"# Bounty $500-2500 Bring up microsoft/phi-1 on Wormhole (N150/N300)\n\n## 📝 Background\n\nThis bounty is for enabling and validating the `microsoft/phi-1` language model on Tenstorrent’s Wormhole hardware. Phi-1 is a transformer-based LLM designed with efficiency and compactness for code and text tasks, making it attractive for research, developers, and edge deployments. By running Phi-1 on Tenstorrent hardware, we aim to demonstrate practical inference, benchmark performance, and establish a production-grade implementation for community use.\n\n## 🎯 What Success Looks Like\n\nTo claim this bounty, contributors must complete all three stages below:\n\n### Stage 1 - Bring Up\n\n- The `microsoft/phi-1` model must compile and run end-to-end inference on Wormhole (N150/N300) with no blocking errors.\n- The model produces coherent output for text generation tasks\n- Integrate `phi-1` support into our [model directory](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/models/demos), maintain the same coding style as used in TT repository and measure performance (see [current benchmarks](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/tt_transformers/PERF.md))\n- Include a simple demo script to run inference and show output.\n\n### Stage 2 - Basic Optimizations\n\n- Store temporary results in L1 memory when possible.\n- Fuse activation functions directly after matmul operations.\n- Apply sharding to tensors where applicable.\n- Leverage existing tt-transformers base modules (avoid duplicating code).\n- Document any parameter tuning or known issues.\n\n### Stage 3 - Deeper Optimization\n\n- Adapt model to exploit TT hardware features, e.g.:\n    - Employ SDPA operator for efficient attention computation.\n    - Minimize unnecessary tensor moves by reordering computation steps.\n- Refactor for modularity and internal code reuse, following production standards.\n\n## 🧭 Guidance & Starting Points\n\n- Use the tt-transformers base in `tt-metal/models/tt_transformers` for model implementation; reuse existing modules where possible.\n- Reference the [model bring up guide](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/model_bring_up.md#model-bring-up).\n- Avoid full codebase duplication—implement in a clean, maintainable way.\n\n## 🔎 Possible Approaches\n\n- Start from an existing transformer implementation in tt-transformers (Llama/Qwen) and adapt for Phi-1.\n- Use modular inheritance to minimize code changes.\n- Profile bottlenecks, optimize memory layout, and use TTNN/tt-metal profiling tools.\n- Reach out in issues or discussions for hardware-specific advice.\n\n## 📊 Result Submission Guidelines Notes\n\nBeyond the model implementation itself, contributors must submit the following proof of work. Feel free to open a PR at any stage for feedback, but payout is only made after all 3 stages are completed.\n\n* Functional model implementation\n* Validation logs showing output correctness and accuracy\n* Performance report + perf header for final review\n\nThe performance report generated will be used as a key piece of information for us to decide if the program is reasonably performant. \n\nLinks:\n- [Link to perf sheet](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/tech_reports/ttnn/TTNN-model-bringup.md#41-performance-sheet)\n- [Perf header](https://docs.tenstorrent.com/tt-metal/latest/ttnn/ttnn/profiling_ttnn_operations.html#perf-report-headers)\n\nFor reference our estimated max throughput for phi-1 is 141 tokens/sec/user on Wormhole. A\n\n---\n\n## 📚 Resources\n\n- [tt-transformers base](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/tree/main/models/tt_transformers)\n- [Model bring up guide](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/model_bring_up.md#model-bring-up)\n- [Phi-1 original paper](https://phi-1-model.github.io/) (if available)\n- [Reference implementation](https://github.com/microsoft/phi-1)\n- [Performance benchmarks](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/blob/main/models/tt_transformers/PERF.md)\n- [Discussion for help](https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/discussions)","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86i9diM","author":{"login":"FL33TW00D"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Happy to give this one a shot!","createdAt":"2025-03-18T16:56:06Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2734020748","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86i9hKH","author":{"login":"thenoahhein"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hey @FL33TW00D \n\nHappy to assign you to this.\n\nBe sure that you read over the [BOUNTY TERMS](https://docs.tenstorrent.com/bounty_terms.html), as you agree to all of them by picking up this issue.\n\nIf we haven't received any communication from you in a two week period, we will re-assign the issue, and you will no longer be eligible for completion of this bounty.\n\nIf you have any questions feel free to ping me here on this issue! Look forward to seeing your submission.","createdAt":"2025-03-18T17:00:24Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"ROCKET","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2734035591","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86mXAhn","author":{"login":"FL33TW00D"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Didn't get around to this until after devday, but it generated its first token today :) \nHaven't hit the Easy benchmark yet, will report back.\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/905e7c41-91a7-4ba0-8fe0-12a52831ec1a)\n","createdAt":"2025-04-09T21:37:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":true,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"ROCKET","users":{"totalCount":2}}],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2791049319","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86mlvsm","author":{"login":"Shubhamsaboo"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Awesome @FL33TW00D! \n\nLooking forward to your PR and first bounty reward.","createdAt":"2025-04-10T19:12:57Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2794912550","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86oOVdZ","author":{"login":"FL33TW00D"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Currently sitting at 14 t/s/u in collaboration with @aminediro.\n","createdAt":"2025-04-22T19:51:09Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[{"content":"THUMBS_UP","users":{"totalCount":1}}],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2822330201","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86oenTt","author":{"login":"Shubhamsaboo"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Anything we can do to help/unblock you?","createdAt":"2025-04-24T07:08:14Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2826597613","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86rQ8WE","author":{"login":"Shubhamsaboo"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Hey @FL33TW00D, any updates on this?","createdAt":"2025-05-12T17:12:35Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2873345412","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86sEqV2","author":{"login":"BenraouaneSoufiane"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@Shubhamsaboo Can I work on this?","createdAt":"2025-05-16T14:35:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2886903158","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86sNHID","author":{"login":"FL33TW00D"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Sorry @Shubhamsaboo I was away for 2 weeks. No longer working on this, we got to 14 tok/s.","createdAt":"2025-05-18T17:43:49Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2889118211","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86sNKFv","author":{"login":"Shubhamsaboo"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"@FL33TW00D do you want to submit that PR? We can consider that under the easy section as I know you have  put a lot of efforts working towards it.","createdAt":"2025-05-18T18:05:20Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2889130351","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86sNMOV","author":{"login":"FL33TW00D"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"@AmineDiro actually did most of the work! if he wants to submit happy for him to claim","createdAt":"2025-05-18T18:22:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2889139093","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86srfx0","author":{"login":"AmineDiro"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@FL33TW00D Did the original work. \n\nHere is the model impl for 14t/s I am still having generation issues \n\n<details>\n  <summary><code>phi1.py</code></summary>\n\n```python\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nimport torch\nimport ttnn\nfrom safetensors import safe_open\nfrom transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoConfig\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch.nn as nn\nfrom enum import Enum\nfrom loguru import logger\nimport time\nfrom typing import Optional\n\n\nclass ForwardMode(Enum):\n    PREFILL = 0\n    DECODE = 1\n\n\nmodel_name = \"microsoft/phi-1\"\n\n\ndef tloader(param, weights, tt_device, dtype=ttnn.bfloat16):\n    torch_t = weights.get_tensor(param)\n\n    if \"mlp\" in param:\n        torch_t = torch_t.T.contiguous()\n\n    return ttnn.as_tensor(\n        torch_t,\n        device=tt_device,\n        layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n        dtype=dtype,\n        memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n    )\n\n\ndef init_kv_cache(config, device, max_batch_size, max_seq_len):\n    \"\"\"\n    Initialize KV cache for a single layer.\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\n        f\"Initializing KV cache with max batch size: {max_batch_size} and max sequence length: {max_seq_len}\"\n    )\n\n    kv_cache = []\n    for _ in range(2):\n        cache_k_or_v = torch.zeros(\n            (\n                max_batch_size,\n                config.num_attention_heads,\n                max_seq_len,\n                config.hidden_size // config.num_attention_heads,\n            )\n        )\n        cache_k_or_v = ttnn.as_tensor(\n            cache_k_or_v,\n            dtype=ttnn.bfloat16,\n            layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n            device=device,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n        )\n        kv_cache.append(cache_k_or_v)\n    return kv_cache\n\n\nclass LightweightModule(ABC):\n    \"\"\"\n    Lightweight version of PyTorch's nn.Module\n    \"\"\"\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def forward(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        raise NotImplementedError(\"should impl\")\n\n    def __call__(self, *args, **kwargs):\n        return self.forward(*args, **kwargs)\n\n\n# class LayerNorm(LightweightModule):\n#     def __init__(self, weight, bias=None, eps=1e-5, compute_kernel_config=None):\n#         super().__init__()\n#         self.weight = weight\n#         self.bias = bias\n#         self.eps = eps\n#         self.compute_kernel_config = compute_kernel_config\n#\n#     def forward(self, x: ttnn.Tensor) -> ttnn.Tensor:\n#         torch_x = ttnn.to_torch(x)\n#         torch_weight = ttnn.to_torch(self.weight)\n#         torch_bias = ttnn.to_torch(self.bias) if self.bias is not None else None\n#\n#         normalized_x = torch.nn.functional.layer_norm(\n#             torch_x,\n#             normalized_shape=torch_x.shape[-1:],\n#             weight=torch_weight,\n#             bias=torch_bias,\n#             eps=self.eps,\n#         )\n#\n#         result = ttnn.from_torch(\n#             normalized_x,\n#             dtype=ttnn.bfloat16,\n#             layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n#             device=tt_device,\n#         )\n#         return result\n\n\nclass LayerNorm(LightweightModule):\n    def __init__(self, weight, bias=None, eps=1e-5, compute_kernel_config=None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.weight = weight\n        self.bias = bias\n        self.eps = eps\n        print(\n            \"LN dtype\",\n            self.weight.dtype,\n            self.bias.dtype if self.bias is not None else None,\n        )\n\n        self.compute_kernel_config = compute_kernel_config\n\n    def forward(self, x: ttnn.Tensor) -> ttnn.Tensor:\n        x = ttnn.typecast(x, dtype=ttnn.float32)\n\n        x = ttnn.layer_norm(\n            x,\n            weight=self.weight,\n            bias=self.bias,\n            epsilon=self.eps,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n            compute_kernel_config=self.compute_kernel_config,\n        )\n\n        x = ttnn.typecast(x, dtype=ttnn.bfloat16)\n        return x\n\n\nclass Embedding(LightweightModule):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        device,\n        weights,\n    ):\n        super().__init__()\n\n        self.weight = tloader(\"model.embed_tokens.weight\", weights, tt_device=device)\n\n    def forward(self, x: ttnn.Tensor) -> ttnn.Tensor:\n        x = ttnn.embedding(\n            x,\n            self.weight,\n            layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n        )\n        return x\n\n\ndef rotate_half(x):\n    \"\"\"Rotates half the hidden dims of the input.\"\"\"\n    x1 = x[..., : x.shape[-1] // 2]\n    x2 = x[..., x.shape[-1] // 2 :]\n    return torch.cat((-x2, x1), dim=-1)\n\n\ndef apply_rotary_pos_emb(q, k, cos, sin, seq_len, past_len, unsqueeze_dim=1):\n    position_ids = gen_position_ids(past_len, seq_len)\n    cos = cos[position_ids].unsqueeze(unsqueeze_dim)\n    sin = sin[position_ids].unsqueeze(unsqueeze_dim)\n    q_embed = (q * cos) + (rotate_half(q) * sin)\n    k_embed = (k * cos) + (rotate_half(k) * sin)\n    return q_embed, k_embed\n\n\nclass RoPE(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, dim, max_position_embeddings=2048, base=10000):\n        super().__init__()\n\n        self.dim = dim\n        self.max_position_embeddings = max_position_embeddings\n        self.base = base\n        inv_freq = 1.0 / (\n            self.base\n            ** (torch.arange(0, self.dim, 2, dtype=torch.int64).float() / self.dim)\n        )\n        self.register_buffer(\"inv_freq\", inv_freq, persistent=False)\n\n        self._set_cos_sin_cache(\n            seq_len=max_position_embeddings,\n            device=inv_freq.device,\n            dtype=torch.get_default_dtype(),\n        )\n\n    def _set_cos_sin_cache(self, seq_len, device, dtype):\n        self.max_seq_len_cached = seq_len\n        t = torch.arange(\n            self.max_seq_len_cached, device=device, dtype=torch.int64\n        ).type_as(self.inv_freq)\n\n        freqs = torch.outer(t, self.inv_freq)\n        emb = torch.cat((freqs, freqs), dim=-1)\n        self.register_buffer(\"cos_cached\", emb.cos().to(dtype), persistent=False)\n        self.register_buffer(\"sin_cached\", emb.sin().to(dtype), persistent=False)\n\n    def forward(self, x, seq_len=None):\n        if seq_len > self.max_seq_len_cached:\n            self._set_cos_sin_cache(seq_len=seq_len, device=x.device, dtype=x.dtype)\n\n        return (\n            self.cos_cached[:seq_len].to(dtype=x.dtype),\n            self.sin_cached[:seq_len].to(dtype=x.dtype),\n        )\n\n\nclass Attention(LightweightModule):\n    def __init__(self, layer_idx, config, weights, device, compute_kernel_config=None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.device = device\n        self.head_dim = config.hidden_size // config.num_attention_heads\n        self.partial_rotary_factor = config.partial_rotary_factor\n        self.rope_theta = config.rope_theta\n        self.max_position_embeddings = config.max_position_embeddings\n\n        self.scaling = self.head_dim**-0.5\n        self.layer_idx = layer_idx\n\n        self.q_weight = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.q_proj.weight\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.q_bias = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.q_proj.bias\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.k_weight = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.k_proj.weight\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.k_bias = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.k_proj.bias\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.v_weight = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.v_proj.weight\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.v_bias = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.v_proj.bias\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.dense = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.dense.weight\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.dense_bias = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.self_attn.dense.bias\", weights, device\n        )\n        self.compute_kernel_config = compute_kernel_config\n\n        self.kv_cache = init_kv_cache(\n            config=config,\n            device=device,\n            max_batch_size=1,\n            max_seq_len=self.max_position_embeddings,\n        )\n\n        self.rotary_emb = RoPE(\n            int(self.partial_rotary_factor * self.head_dim),\n            max_position_embeddings=self.max_position_embeddings,\n            base=self.rope_theta,\n        )\n\n    def forward(\n        self,\n        hidden_states,\n        past_len=0,\n    ):\n        input_shape = (hidden_states.shape[0], hidden_states.shape[1])\n        hidden_shape = (*input_shape, -1, self.head_dim)\n\n        forward_mode = ForwardMode.PREFILL if past_len == 0 else ForwardMode.DECODE\n\n        query_states = ttnn.linear(\n            hidden_states,\n            self.q_weight,\n            bias=self.q_bias,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n            transpose_b=True,\n        )\n\n        key_states = ttnn.linear(\n            hidden_states,\n            self.k_weight,\n            bias=self.k_bias,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n            transpose_b=True,\n        )\n\n        value_states = ttnn.linear(\n            hidden_states,\n            self.v_weight,\n            bias=self.v_bias,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n            transpose_b=True,\n        )\n\n        query_states = ttnn.transpose(ttnn.reshape(query_states, hidden_shape), 1, 2)\n        key_states = ttnn.transpose(ttnn.reshape(key_states, hidden_shape), 1, 2)\n        value_states = ttnn.transpose(ttnn.reshape(value_states, hidden_shape), 1, 2)\n\n        kv_seq_len = key_states.shape[2]\n        query_states = ttnn.to_torch(query_states)\n        key_states = ttnn.to_torch(key_states)\n        value_states = ttnn.to_torch(value_states)\n\n        cos, sin = self.rotary_emb(value_states, seq_len=past_len + kv_seq_len)\n\n        query_rot, query_pass = (\n            query_states[..., : self.rotary_emb.dim],\n            query_states[..., self.rotary_emb.dim :],\n        )\n        key_rot, key_pass = (\n            key_states[..., : self.rotary_emb.dim],\n            key_states[..., self.rotary_emb.dim :],\n        )\n\n        query_rot, key_rot = apply_rotary_pos_emb(\n            query_rot, key_rot, cos, sin, kv_seq_len, past_len\n        )\n\n        query_states = torch.cat((query_rot, query_pass), dim=-1)\n        key_states = torch.cat((key_rot, key_pass), dim=-1)\n\n        query_states = ttnn.from_torch(\n            query_states,\n            dtype=ttnn.bfloat16,\n            layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n            device=self.device,\n        )\n        key_states = ttnn.from_torch(\n            key_states,\n            dtype=ttnn.bfloat16,\n            layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n            device=self.device,\n        )\n        value_states = ttnn.from_torch(\n            value_states,\n            dtype=ttnn.bfloat16,\n            layout=ttnn.TILE_LAYOUT,\n            device=self.device,\n        )\n\n        k_cache, v_cache = self.kv_cache\n        if forward_mode == ForwardMode.PREFILL:\n            ttnn.kv_cache.fill_cache_for_user_(k_cache, key_states, batch_index=0)\n            ttnn.kv_cache.fill_cache_for_user_(v_cache, value_states, batch_index=0)\n        else:\n            ttnn.kv_cache.update_cache_for_token_(\n                k_cache, key_states, update_index=past_len, batch_offset=0\n            )\n            ttnn.kv_cache.update_cache_for_token_(\n                v_cache, value_states, update_index=past_len, batch_offset=0\n            )\n\n        keys = k_cache[:, :, : past_len + kv_seq_len, :]\n        values = v_cache[:, :, : past_len + kv_seq_len, :]\n\n        if forward_mode == ForwardMode.PREFILL:\n            attn_output = ttnn.transformer.scaled_dot_product_attention(\n                query_states,\n                keys,\n                values,\n                attn_mask=None,\n                is_causal=True,\n                scale=self.scaling,\n            )\n        else:\n            keys_t = ttnn.transpose(keys, -1, -2)\n            attn_scores = ttnn.matmul(query_states, keys_t)\n            attn_scores = ttnn.mul(attn_scores, self.scaling)\n            attn_weights = ttnn.softmax(attn_scores, dim=-1)\n            attn_output = ttnn.matmul(attn_weights, values)\n\n        attn_output = ttnn.transpose(attn_output, 1, 2)\n        attn_output = ttnn.reshape(attn_output, (*input_shape, -1))\n\n        attn_output = ttnn.linear(\n            attn_output,\n            self.dense,\n            bias=self.dense_bias,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n            transpose_b=True,\n        )\n\n        return attn_output, None\n\n\nclass MLP(LightweightModule):\n    def __init__(self, layer_idx, weights, device, compute_kernel_config=None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.fc1 = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.mlp.fc1.weight\", weights, tt_device=device\n        )\n        self.fc1_bias = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.mlp.fc1.bias\", weights, tt_device=device\n        )\n        self.fc2 = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.mlp.fc2.weight\", weights, tt_device=device\n        )\n        self.fc2_bias = tloader(\n            f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.mlp.fc2.bias\", weights, tt_device=device\n        )\n        self.layer_idx = layer_idx\n        self.compute_kernel_config = compute_kernel_config\n\n    def forward(self, hidden_states: ttnn.Tensor) -> ttnn.Tensor:\n        hidden_states = ttnn.linear(\n            hidden_states,\n            self.fc1,\n            bias=self.fc1_bias,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n        )\n        hidden_states = ttnn.gelu(hidden_states)\n        hidden_states = ttnn.linear(\n            hidden_states,\n            self.fc2,\n            bias=self.fc2_bias,\n            memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG,\n        )\n        return hidden_states\n\n\nclass DecoderLayer(LightweightModule):\n    def __init__(self, layer_idx, config, weights, device, compute_kernel_config):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.attention = Attention(layer_idx, config, weights, device)\n        self.device = device\n        self.mlp = MLP(layer_idx, weights, device, compute_kernel_config)\n        self.layer_idx = layer_idx\n        self.input_layernorm = LayerNorm(\n            tloader(\n                f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.input_layernorm.weight\",\n                weights,\n                device,\n                dtype=ttnn.float32,\n            ),\n            tloader(\n                f\"model.layers.{layer_idx}.input_layernorm.bias\",\n                weights,\n                device,\n                dtype=ttnn.float32,\n            ),\n            config.layer_norm_eps,\n            compute_kernel_config,\n        )\n\n    def forward(self, hidden_states: ttnn.Tensor, past_len) -> ttnn.Tensor:\n        residual = hidden_states\n        hidden_states = self.input_layernorm(hidden_states)\n        attn_output, _ = self.attention(\n            hidden_states,\n            past_len=past_len,\n        )\n        ffn_output = self.mlp(hidden_states)\n        return ttnn.add(ttnn.add(residual, attn_output), ffn_output)\n\n\nclass PhiModel(LightweightModule):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        device,\n        weights,\n        config,\n    ):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.compute_kernel_config = ttnn.WormholeComputeKernelConfig(\n            math_fidelity=ttnn.MathFidelity.HiFi2,\n            math_approx_mode=False,\n            fp32_dest_acc_en=True,\n            packer_l1_acc=False,\n        )\n\n        self.device = device\n        self.embedding = Embedding(device, weights)\n        self.layers = [\n            DecoderLayer(layer_idx, config, weights, device, self.compute_kernel_config)\n            for layer_idx in range(config.num_hidden_layers)\n        ]\n\n        self.lm_head = tloader(\"lm_head.weight\", weights, device)\n        self.final_layer_norm = LayerNorm(\n            tloader(\n                \"model.final_layernorm.weight\", weights, device, dtype=ttnn.bfloat16\n            ),\n            tloader(\"model.final_layernorm.bias\", weights, device, dtype=ttnn.bfloat16),\n            config.layer_norm_eps,\n            self.compute_kernel_config,\n        )\n        self.past_len = 0\n\n    def forward(self, input_ids: ttnn.Tensor) -> ttnn.Tensor:\n        if input_ids.shape[1] > 1:\n            self.past_len = 0\n        x = self.embedding(input_ids)\n        for layer in self.layers:\n            x = layer(x, self.past_len)\n        x = self.final_layer_norm(x)\n        x = ttnn.linear(\n            x, self.lm_head, memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG, transpose_b=True\n        )\n        self.past_len += input_ids.shape[1]\n        return x\n\n\n# s = existing sequence length\n# t = current generation length (1 for decode)\ndef gen_position_ids(s, t):\n    position_ids = torch.arange(s, s + t, dtype=torch.long)\n    position_ids = position_ids.unsqueeze(0)\n    return position_ids\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    torch_device = torch.device(\"cpu\")\n    weights = safe_open(\"phi.safetensors\", framework=\"pt\", device=\"cpu\")\n    tt_device = ttnn.open_device(device_id=0)\n    ttnn.enable_program_cache(tt_device)\n    # tt_device = ttnn.open_mesh_device(ttnn.MeshShape(1,2))\n    # tt_device.enable_async(True)\n\n    prompt = \"Do not go gentle into \"\n    tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name, trust_remote_code=True)\n    config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(model_name)\n    inputs = tokenizer(prompt, return_tensors=\"pt\")\n    input_ids = inputs[\"input_ids\"]\n    print(\"Input ids: \", input_ids)\n    generated_tokens = input_ids.clone()\n\n    model = PhiModel(tt_device, weights, config)\n    max_new_tokens = 50\n\n    start_time = time.time()\n    for _ in range(max_new_tokens):\n        tt_inputs = ttnn.as_tensor(\n            input_ids, device=tt_device, memory_config=ttnn.DRAM_MEMORY_CONFIG\n        )\n        output = model(tt_inputs)\n\n        torch_output = ttnn.to_torch(output)\n        next_token_logits = torch_output[:, 0, :]\n        next_token = torch.argmax(next_token_logits, dim=-1).unsqueeze(-1)\n        generated_tokens = torch.cat((generated_tokens, next_token), dim=1)\n        input_ids = next_token\n        print(\"NEXT TOKEN:\", next_token.item())\n\n    end_time = time.time()\n    tok_per_sec = (input_ids.shape[-1] + max_new_tokens) / (end_time - start_time)\n    logger.info(f\"Generation time: {end_time - start_time:.2f}s\")\n    logger.info(\n        f\"Tokens per second: {tok_per_sec:.2f}\",\n    )\n    logger.debug(f\"Generated tokens: {generated_tokens}\")\n    txt = tokenizer.decode(generated_tokens[0], skip_special_tokens=True)\n    print(f\"\\n\\nFull generated text: {txt}\")\n\n    ttnn.close_device(tt_device)\n```\n</details>\n","createdAt":"2025-05-21T08:32:42Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2897083508","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86ssZzf","author":{"login":"FL33TW00D"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"@Shubhamsaboo it's probably not bounty worthy, but we had fun! ","createdAt":"2025-05-21T09:49:30Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2897321183","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86sv8oK","author":{"login":"Shubhamsaboo"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"Haha, you guys are awesome! ","createdAt":"2025-05-21T14:51:00Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment-2898250250","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOI9Wqc86tIvFW","author":{"login":"Shubhamsaboo"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"I am reopening this bounty.","createdAt":"2025-05-23T15:03:54Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/tenstorrent/tt-metal/issues/18287#issuecomment